<Project>

  <!--
    Workaround for a C# Dev Kit / MSBuild incompatibility that breaks the
    "Build RELEASE" (and any other) msbuild.exe invocation of this solution.

    C# Dev Kit injects the environment variable

        CustomAfterMicrosoftCommonTargets = <csdevkit>\dist\msbuild\Microsoft.NET.ProjectData.targets

    (plus EnableProjectDataOnBuild=true) into VS Code's integrated terminals.
    That targets file loads Microsoft.NET.ProjectData.Tasks.dll, which is built
    against .NET 10 and therefore cannot be loaded by the .NET Framework based
    MSBuild that ships with Visual Studio 2022. Every build then fails with:

        error MSB4062: ... Microsoft.NET.ProjectData.Tasks.WriteProjectDataSliceTask
        ... "System.Runtime, Version=10.0.0.0" ... could not be found.

    dotnet build is unaffected (the .NET host resolves the newer framework
    assembly); only msbuild.exe hits this.

    Disabling the opportunistic project-data write during ordinary builds keeps
    the task from being loaded here. C# Dev Kit still produces project data via
    its own design-time builds, so editor features are unaffected.
    Delete this file if C# Dev Kit stops injecting that targets file.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <EnableProjectDataOnBuild>false</EnableProjectDataOnBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
